-- 2026-11-09: Caring Companions now hires caregivers 21 or older (her rule; it was 18).
-- Only Cara's K117 answer changes, and only when it still differs. Same text as supabase/knowledge/cara-2026-10-27.mjs.
update public.kb_items set answer = 'We ask for at least one year of paid caregiving experience. Work at home, in a nursing home, assisted living or a hospital counts, and so does being paid to care for a family member. Wellness Care roles need no license. Advanced Care roles are for licensed CNAs. You must be 21 or older and able to work in the United States. For anything else, apply at mo-care.com/apply and we will talk it through.', version = version + 1, updated_at = now(),
  verified_on = '2026-11-09', verified_by = 'Samantha 11-09: hiring is 21 and up'
  where id = 'K117' and answer is distinct from 'We ask for at least one year of paid caregiving experience. Work at home, in a nursing home, assisted living or a hospital counts, and so does being paid to care for a family member. Wellness Care roles need no license. Advanced Care roles are for licensed CNAs. You must be 21 or older and able to work in the United States. For anything else, apply at mo-care.com/apply and we will talk it through.';
